{"name":"Thunder Chi","hex":"#aac4d4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thunder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The loud rumbling, cracking, or crashing sound caused by expansion of rapidly heated air around a lightning bolt.","A deep, rumbling noise resembling thunder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce thunder; to sound, rattle, or roar, as a discharge of atmospheric electricity.","To make a noise like thunder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder"},{"term":"chi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Chinese."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The twenty-second letter of the Classical and Modern Greek alphabets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thunder","blocks":[{"text":"Thunder is the sound caused by lightning. Depending upon the distance from and nature of the lightning, it can range from a long, low rumble to a sudden, loud crack. The sudden increase in temperature and hence pressure caused by the lightning produces rapid expansion of the air in the path of a lightning bolt. In turn, this expansion of air creates a sonic shock wave, often referred to as a \"thunderclap\" or \"peal of thunder\". The scientific study of thunder is known as brontology and the irrational fear (phobia) of thunder is called brontophobia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder","wikidata":"Q83301"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"thunder":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Back_ache-thunder.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/34/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Ba